{
 "eyebrow": "Strategies · Backtest Review 2023–2025",
 "as_of": "2026-11-10",
 "title": "Every strategy on its own $10,000 account, 2023–2025",
 "lede": {
  "technical": "93 strategies, 98,731 trades, costs deducted. Each strategy is replayed on its own $10,000 account with fixed-fractional risk (a set % of current equity per trade) so profits and losses compound. 22 of 93 were profitable over the three years. The live book (1 qualified + 4 designated) lost; the SHADOW forward-test set made money.",
  "plain": "We replayed every strategy we have ever worked with, one by one, as if each had its own $10,000 account from January 2023 to December 2025. 22 of 93 ended up making money. The strategies trading today would have lost about half the account at 0.5% risk per trade; the small group being paper-tested now would have grown it."
 },
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "headline",
   "nav": "Headline",
   "kicker": "Result",
   "title": "What the three years say",
   "body": {
    "technical": "Live book at 0.5% risk: $10,000 → $5,005 (max drawdown 52.8%). SHADOW set at 1% risk: $10,000 → $14,138 (max drawdown 16.7%, ~12%/yr). Everything traded at once is ruinous: the losing high-frequency strategies dominate the trade count.",
    "plain": "The book trading today would have shrunk $10,000 to about $5,005. The paper-test group would have grown it to about $14,138. Turning everything on at once would have emptied the account."
   },
   "callouts": [
    {
     "tone": "good",
     "title": "Best single strategies (1% risk)",
     "text": "nnfx_backtrader +29.9% with a 4.1% max drawdown (and its research twin nnfx_backtrader_fx +24.7%), weekly_day_reversal_ea +29.3% (but a 36% drawdown), ma_crossover_swing +24.6%, post_fomc_drift +17.4%. Most trade less than once a week."
    },
    {
     "tone": "bad",
     "title": "The live book loses",
     "text": "Of the five strategies routed live today, only nnfx_backtrader made money. precision_swing −45.9%, inside_bar_reversal −45.4%, strong_weak_analysis −27.6%, h4_crossover_21_89_macd (qualified) −14.9% over three years at 1% risk."
    },
    {
     "tone": "warn",
     "title": "Selection is not done here",
     "text": "This page records what each strategy would have made. Which ones to combine into a book is an owner decision taken after reading it — see Open decisions."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "method",
   "nav": "Method",
   "kicker": "How it was run",
   "title": "Method and assumptions",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "technical": "**Trades.** Legacy fleet (41 strategies): `fact_trade_outcomes`, engine position_engine_v2, `r_multiple` net of a round-trip cost. Strategy House (52): the strategy's pre-registered `one_shot_2023` run where one exists, otherwise a review run (`kind=explore`, 2023-01-01 → 2025-12-31, runs 1179–1221 on 2026-11-10), `r_net` net of spread, slippage and financing.",
     "plain": "Every trade comes from our own backtest engine with trading costs already taken off."
    },
    {
     "technical": "**Account.** $10,000 start; each trade risks a fixed % of current equity (0.25%, 0.5%, 1%, 2%); equity updates when a trade closes. Yearly return = year-end balance vs. the previous year-end on one continuous account. Max drawdown = largest fall from a peak, in %.",
     "plain": "Each trade risks a slice of whatever the account holds at the time, so wins and losses compound."
    },
    {
     "technical": "**Leverage.** Risk per trade is the real lever; leverage only has to be high enough to open the position. Margin is not modelled (legacy rows carry no stop distance). The \"max open\" column shows how many trades were open at once — open risk = that × risk per trade.",
     "plain": "How much you risk per trade decides the result. Leverage just has to allow the trade to be opened."
    },
    {
     "technical": "**Prop firm** (generic two-step, not a specific firm): $100,000 account, phase 1 +8%, phase 2 +5%, daily loss 5%, max loss 10% of the starting balance, 80% profit split, $540 fee. A fresh attempt starts on the first of every month from Jan 2023 to Jun 2025 (30 attempts); a funded account pays out profit above +1% and keeps trading to end-2025.",
     "plain": "We tried a typical prop-firm challenge 30 times, one start per month, and counted how often each strategy passed and what it paid out after the fee."
    }
   ],
   "callouts": [
    {
     "tone": "warn",
     "title": "What makes these numbers look better than reality",
     "text": "1) Legacy fleet results are not out-of-sample; their code was written after much of this history. 2) The demo cap (10 open trades, 16 a day) is not applied. 3) Prop daily loss counts closed trades only; firms count open losses too. 4) h4_box_breakout's legacy rows are summer-only (fixed 2026-11-10). 5) The live gatekeeper and probability gate are not applied — every signal is taken."
    }
   ]
  },
